<NPCCharacters>

  <!-- Spider Rider line: three goblin cavalry rungs, one skin each (#616, 2026-09-17), the warg
       line's shape (dg_warg_scout -> raider -> skirmisher). Spider Rider (L21) rides the Giant
       Spider (spider_mount_a, dark, scale 1.0); Brown Spider Rider (L26) the Brown Spider
       (spider_mount_brown, scale 1.10); Pale Spider Rider (L31) the Pale Spider (spider_mount_pale,
       scale 1.25). Size lives on the ITEM (body_length), the three items share Monster.spider and
       every speed stat, and every C# spider seam keys on the Monster, so the rungs differ in
       rider kit, skills and mount size only. Five levels per rung keeps the engine tier rising
       (UPGRADE_TIER_COLLAPSE); the levels and the kit steps (light, medium, heavy) are the warg
       line's own from its second rung up (dg_warg_raider 21, skirmisher 26, red_fang 31).
       Replaces the old detached-spider anchor (dg_uruk race, Wanderer) with the horse-slot
       mount pattern — same as taom_war_elephant / harad_mahout. The engine spawns TWO agents:
         1. The goblin rider (FromCharacterObj, humanoid, race=goblin)
         2. The spider mount (FromHorseObj, Monster.spider, non-humanoid)
       No C# spawn interception required; vanilla cavalry spawn handles both.

       occupation="Soldier" → IsSoldier=true → appears in Custom Battle picker (intended;
       the goblin-riding-a-spider is a valid custom-battle unit). The old "Wanderer" trick
       was needed only because the old approach embedded the spider in the rider's visual.

       The detached-spider machinery (Patch45 spawn-swap + native wield guards) was DELETED
       2026-06-10 — the rider equips weapons + joins formations via plain vanilla cavalry
       rules. The spider mount auto-bites via SpiderBehaviorTree (attached by
       SpiderMissionBehavior, keyed on Monster.StringId=="spider").

       VolunteerRecruitmentService carries this ID in the Dol Guldur settlement pools at
       weight 1 (rare fief recruit; intentionally absent from the clan pools). -->
  <NPCCharacter id="taom_spider_creature"
                race="goblin"
                default_group="Cavalry"
                level="21"
                is_hero="false"
                is_basic_troop="false"
                occupation="Soldier"
                culture="Culture.dolguldur"
                name="{=taom_spider_creature_name}Spider Rider">
    <face><face_key_template value="BodyProperty.fighter_goblin" /></face>
    <skills>
      <skill id="Athletics" value="80" />
      <skill id="Riding" value="100" />
      <skill id="OneHanded" value="100" />
      <skill id="Polearm" value="80" />
    </skills>
    <upgrade_targets>
